# Allowlist for `make security` (govulncheck).
#
# One ID per line. Accepts Go vuln DB IDs (GO-YYYY-NNNN), GHSA IDs,
# or CVE IDs — the wrapper matches against the OSV record's id and aliases.
#
# Lines starting with `#` are comments. Use them to document *why* each entry
# is allowlisted so a reviewer can re-evaluate later.

# GHSA-x744-4wpc-v9h2 — Moby AuthZ plugin bypass on oversized request bodies.
# Affects dockerd when an AuthorizationPlugin is configured. qtap imports the
# Docker client library only (github.com/docker/docker/{client,api/types/...})
# to talk to a Docker socket; it never runs the daemon or authz code paths.
# No fix is available on the github.com/docker/docker or github.com/moby/moby
# module paths — the patched release is only on github.com/moby/moby/v2.
# Covers Dependabot alerts #19 and #21. Revisit when docker/docker publishes
# a v29 Go module.
GO-2026-4887

# GHSA-pxq6-2prw-chj9 — Moby off-by-one in plugin privilege validation.
# Affects dockerd's plugin privilege check. qtap does not run the daemon or
# install Docker plugins; the vulnerable code path is unreachable from our
# client-only usage. Same upstream fix situation as GO-2026-4887: patched on
# github.com/moby/moby/v2 only, not on the github.com/docker/docker module.
# Covers Dependabot alerts #18 and #20.
GO-2026-4883

# These Docker archive/copy advisories affect dockerd's server-side archive
# extraction and bind-mount handling. qtap imports github.com/docker/docker as
# an API client and does not embed or run the daemon implementation. The
# github.com/docker/docker module has no patched release; fixes are published
# only on github.com/moby/moby/v2. Revisit when the Docker client module moves
# to that path or publishes a fixed version.
GO-2026-5617
GO-2026-5668
GO-2026-5746

# golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is deprecated as a package, but qtap does not
# import it. govulncheck reports this as a module-only finding because qtap
# uses other x/crypto packages through validator. There is no fixed x/crypto
# version; revisit if openpgp ever appears in `go list -deps -test ./...`.
GO-2026-5932
